+# Performance history
+
+Dated entries for hook/path costs that changed materially. Each entry states
+what was measured, not an estimate, and says so when only an estimate exists.
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+Before: quick_check ran on the read path on every `SessionStart`.
+
+After: quick_check was taken off the read path; the result is now cached and
+checked in O(1), with a trigger-maintained `fts_rows` counter and a body
+`CHECK` added to the schema at the same time (see
+`crates/muninn-core/src/health.rs`, `crates/muninn-core/src/db.rs`).
+
+| | cost |
+|---|---|
+| Before (quick_check on read path) | 11.9 ms |
+| After (quick_check off read path, `fts_rows` counter, body `CHECK`) | 1.05 ms |
+
+These numbers come from a prior session's tool-observed measurement (trust 1,
+not yet corroborated by an exit code or commit in this checkout), not from a
+benchmark artifact committed to this repository — `grep` over `research/` and
+`crates/muninn-bench/` found no matching figures here. The source note does
+not state which percentile these are (this doc assumes p50, matching how the
+task refers to them) or the exact record count of the store used, so treat
+the "5k-record store" framing as the assumed context, not a confirmed detail.
+
+`crates/muninn-bench` ships a `perf` subcommand (`muninn-bench perf --records
+5000`) that reports p50/p95/p99 for `hook SessionStart` directly and would
+give an unambiguous, reproducible number for the current (after) state. It
+was not run for this entry: building the workspace in this session required
+an approval this environment did not grant. Re-running it, and — if the
+pre-change code is still reachable in history — running it again before the
+`quick_check` change, would replace the estimate-flagged parts of this entry
+with a fully measured one.
